  "cil_liability": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposed parking arrangement would provide a safe, functional and convenient form of access, parking and pedestrian movement. In the absence of swept path analysis or other suitable evidence, it has not been demonstrated that vehicles can safely enter, manoeuvre within and exit the site without conflict with pedestrian movements or prejudice to highway safety. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies T2, T6.1 and T7 of the London Plan (2021), Policies CP24, CP25 and CP26 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD45, DMD47 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The applicant has failed to provide sufficient information, including a robust parking stress survey, to demonstrate that the additional parking demand generated by the proposed 6-person House in Multiple Occupation can be accommodated without resulting in unacceptable pressure on surrounding on-street parking provision or adverse impacts on the operation of the local highway network. In the absence of this information, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the proposal complies with Policies T2 and T6 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DMD45 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).\r\r"
  ]
